<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L1_3" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L1_3">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L1_3" name="3 Processing &amp; Beneficiation (L1)" processRef="Process_L1_3"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L1_3" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Pillar 3 L2 process areas. 3.3 thickens both concentrate and tailings; thickened tailings go to 3.5. 3.4 runs alongside from its own shift start and 3.6 from site water demand. Associations show data and water links: 3.2 and 3.3 to 3.4 (measurement data), 3.5 to 3.6 (pond, seepage and drainage water). 3.1 also supplies 3.4 (crusher feed, MP-01) and 3.3 supplies 3.6 (recovered water); not drawn, to keep the lines clear.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L1_3">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L1_3_acc" name="Chief Metallurgist / Metallurgical Accounting Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L1_3_e4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L1_3_s3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L1_3_3_4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L1_3_ops" name="Control Room Operator / DCS Auto-control / Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L1_3_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L1_3_3_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L1_3_3_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L1_3_3_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Par_L1_3_f</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L1_3_e1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L1_3_tw" name="Tailings &amp; Water Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L1_3_3_5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L1_3_e2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L1_3_s2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L1_3_3_6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L1_3_e3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L1_3_e4" name="Monthly metal accounting report filed">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_11</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L1_3_s3" name="Shift start">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L1_3_3_4" name="3.4 Metallurgical Accounting &amp; Quality">
      <bpmn:documentation>L2/L3 Process Area. Systematic collection of representative samples, chemical analysis, and mass balance closure across the plant. Metallurgical accounting is the mechanism by which all mass flows, grades, and recoveries are reconciled to verify and report plant performance. This process area is governed end-to-end by AMIRA P754 and all 10 of its principles apply within it.
ISA-95 level: 2–3
Actors: Chief Metallurgist; Metallurgist; Plant Chemist; Metallurgical Accounting Analyst
Standard alignment: AMIRA P754 (all 10 principles); ISA-95 Levels 2, 3
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (shift_mass_balance, metallurgical_accounting_report)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L1_3_s" name="ROM ore at crusher (CTP-1)">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="Msg_L1_3_s"/>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L1_3_3_1" name="3.1 Comminution">
      <bpmn:documentation>L2 Process Area. Progressive size reduction of ROM ore from run-of-mine fragmentation (typically P80 150–250 mm) to a target grind size suitable for flotation (P80 75–150 µm depending on ore and circuit). Encompasses primary crushing, secondary/tertiary crushing and screening where applicable, SAG and ball milling, and hydrocyclone classification.
ISA-95 level: 0–3
Actors: Plant Metallurgist; Control Room Operator; DCS Auto-control
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–3; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 5
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series); Curated (process_node, equipment_operating_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L1_3_3_2" name="3.2 Concentration (Flotation)">
      <bpmn:documentation>L2 Process Area. Selective separation of valuable sulphide minerals (e.g., chalcopyrite, sphalerite, galena, molybdenite) from gangue using froth flotation. Air bubbles attach to mineral surfaces made hydrophobic by reagents; the loaded froth overflows as concentrate while depressed minerals report to tailings. This is the primary value-creation process in the plant — metal recovery and concentrate grade are the defining performance variables. The area combines two patterns: one or more Flotation Circuits (3.2.2), in sequence (each fed by the previous circuit's tailings) or in parallel on split feeds, and an optional Concentrate Separation (3.2.3) of a bulk concentrate. Each circuit's concentrate is saleable, a bulk concentrate for separation, or a waste concentrate (e.g., pyrite removed to make low-sulphur tailings). The circuit set, order, destinations and reagent scheme are configuration, not separate processes, and may change by ore-type campaign.
ISA-95 level: 0–3
Actors: Control Room Operator; Metallurgist; DCS Auto-control
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–3; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 5, 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series); Curated (concentrate_production_record, process_measurement_point)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L1_3_3_3" name="3.3 Dewatering &amp; Product Handling">
      <bpmn:documentation>L2 Process Area. Removes water from flotation products. Saleable concentrates are thickened, filtered to the commercial moisture specification (typically 8–12% for copper and 6–10% for zinc or lead concentrate, by contract) and, where specified, dried and packed. The final tailings are thickened to the density the deposition method needs and handed to Tailings Management (3.5). Water recovered by thickening and filtration is handed to Water Management (3.6).
ISA-95 level: 0–2
Actors: Control Room Operator; DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 5, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series); Curated (concentrate_production_record, process_measurement_point)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Par_L1_3_f">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_5</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L1_3_e1" name="Concentrate to storage (CTP-2)">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="Msg_L1_3_e1"/>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L1_3_3_5" name="3.5 Tailings Management">
      <bpmn:documentation>L2 Process Area. Transports thickened tailings from the plant to the Tailings Storage Facility (TSF), classifies them into sand and fines where the embankment is built with tailings sand, deposits tailings in the impoundment, builds and raises the embankment, and monitors storage and safety margins. The TSF is the final sink of the plant mass balance and the main store of reclaim water (3.6.2). A TSF receives material for the whole mine life, so its inventory, water and geometry change continuously.
ISA-95 level: 0–3
Actors: Tailings Operator; Control Room Operator; Construction Supervisor / Surveyor; Tailings Facility Engineer
Standard alignment: GISTM (2020); ICMM tailings governance; ISA-95 Levels 0–3; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 5, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series); Curated (tailings_deposition_record, construction_placement_record, facility_survey_record, tsf_inventory_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L1_3_e2" name="Tailings stored in TSF">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L1_3_s2" name="Site water demand">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L1_3_3_6" name="3.6 Water Management">
      <bpmn:documentation>L2 Process Area. Supplies, recovers, distributes and accounts for the water the plant and the tailings facility use. Water enters as makeup water from a configured source, treated where required; it is recovered by thickening and filtration (3.3), reclaimed from the TSF pond and recovered from seepage and drainage; it is blended into process water and distributed to users; and it is accounted for in a periodic site water balance that counts each volume once.
ISA-95 level: 1–4
Actors: Water Operator; Control Room Operator; Tailings Operator; Environmental Officer; Water Balance Analyst
Standard alignment: MCA Water Accounting Framework; ICMM water reporting guidance; ISA-95 Levels 1–4
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: water_flow_telemetry, pond_level_telemetry); Curated (water_transfer_record, water_balance_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L1_3_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L1_3_e3" name="Period water balance published">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L1_3_9</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_1" sourceRef="Start_L1_3_s" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_2" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_1" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_3" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_2" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_4" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_3" targetRef="Par_L1_3_f"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_5" sourceRef="Par_L1_3_f" targetRef="End_L1_3_e1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_6" sourceRef="Par_L1_3_f" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_5"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_7" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_5" targetRef="End_L1_3_e2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_8" sourceRef="Start_L1_3_s2" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_6"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_9" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_6" targetRef="End_L1_3_e3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_10" sourceRef="Start_L1_3_s3" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L1_3_11" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_4" targetRef="End_L1_3_e4"/>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_L1_3_12" associationDirection="One" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_2" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_4"/>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_L1_3_13" associationDirection="One" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_3" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_4"/>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_L1_3_14" associationDirection="One" sourceRef="Sub_L1_3_3_5" targetRef="Sub_L1_3_3_6"/>
  </bpmn:process>
